    {"n":"1","text":"Treat this as an unloaded prototype. The actual clamp profile and camera socket depth are unknown. If you cannot perform the following checks, use a compatible commercial replacement instead.","parts":[]},
    {"n":"2","text":"Print profile_coupon in the specified orientation, 0.2 mm layers, six walls and 100% infill. No supports. Remove brim or elephant-foot material without changing the angled contact surfaces.","parts":["profile_coupon"]},
    {"n":"3","text":"With no camera attached, open the clamp and invert the coupon into it, X along jaws. Check both angled faces seat evenly beneath the lips, with no rocking or interference from the upper shoulder. Tighten normally by hand. Try to lift, twist and slide it out by hand. Reject any release, cracking, stress whitening, edge-only contact or jaw travel bottoming. If it fails, stop: the assumed profile needs measured redesign, not extra tightening.","parts":["profile_coupon"]},
    {"n":"4","text":"Only after the coupon fits, print camera_plate broad camera face down, 0.2 mm layers, six walls and 100% infill, no supports. Inspect for poor layer bonding or warping. Fit the full plate into the empty clamp and repeat all unloaded checks, including full-length seating and bolt-head clearance. There are no anti-slide stop screws: always support the plate when loosening the clamp.","parts":["camera_plate"]},
    {"n":"5","text":"Insert camera_bolt through the recess from the dovetail side. Its head must bear flat on the recessed floor and be fully below the outer plate face. Confirm you can tighten it using its actual drive without damaging it; stop if the recess prevents tool access. Measure the actual screw projection above the camera face; expected approximately 4 mm.","parts":["camera_plate"],"hardware":["camera_bolt"],"tool":"Calipers and the drive tool matching the salvaged bolt"},
    {"n":"6","text":"Before threading into the camera, establish usable socket depth using the camera manufacturer's specification or a careful blunt nonmetallic depth probe; a probe alone does not establish usable thread length. Require at least 1 mm clearance beyond the screw tip and at least three full turns of real engagement before the plate seats. Do not proceed if either is uncertain. Never force a screw to check depth; never substitute an M6 screw. If dimensions fail, redesign screw_grip or obtain a suitable commercial screw/plate; do not improvise with unlisted spacers.","parts":["camera_plate"],"hardware":["camera_bolt"]},
    {"n":"7","text":"On a padded surface, hold the camera securely, hand-start the bolt and tighten gently with the correct drive. Verify plate seats flat without rocking or rotation and no controls, lens or doors are obstructed. If the screw stops before the plate seats, remove it immediately: it may be bottoming out. Do not overcome movement by overtightening PLA.","parts":["camera_plate"],"hardware":["camera_bolt"],"tool":"Drive tool matching the salvaged bolt"},
